OL,3,GNEWSAStudent who spells by blinking is
OL,4,Adenied chance to sit exam
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt takes Romi Loffler about half an
OL,7,Fhour to write a sentence, spelling it
OL,8,Fout one letter at a time by blinking.
OL,10,FThe 21-year-old, from Netherlee in East
OL,11,FRenfrewshire, has Rett Syndrome, a
OL,12,Fgenetic neurological disorder which
OL,13,Fleaves her unable to speak or move and
OL,14,Fcomes with a range of health problems
OL,15,Fincluding epilepsy.
OL,17,FFor years, people with the condition
OL,18,Fwere assumed to have profound learning
OL,19,Fdisabilities but Romi, who uses special
OL,20,Feye-gaze technology to communicate, is
OL,21,Fhoping to challenge that belief.
OL,23,APub: 12-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,424,420,260,160,0,100
